  "abstract": "Covers the W3C Verifiable Credentials Data Model v2.0 (Recommendation, 15 May 2025) with its companion Recommendations, each the current line of its own family: Securing Verifiable Credentials using JOSE and COSE, Verifiable Credential Data Integrity 1.0 with the EdDSA and ECDSA cryptosuites (and the BBS cryptosuite, still a Candidate Recommendation Draft), and Bitstring Status List v1.0. VC Data Model 1.1 is a legacy line with upgrade steps; the VC Data Model 2.1, Data Integrity 1.1 and Bitstring Status List 1.1 Working Drafts are tracked as previews. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references/ splits versions, the data model and JSON-LD processing, securing mechanisms, status lists, and verification, validation, security and privacy.",
